.TH FHICL-SUMMARY 1 "2026-10-06" "mu2ebintools v1_01_21" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
fhicl-summary \- summarise the structure of an art job configuration
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B fhicl-summary
.RB [ \-v | \-vv ]
.I file.fcl
.br
.B fhicl-summary
.RB { \-h | \-\-help }
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B fhicl-summary
parses
.I file.fcl
with fhiclcpp, builds the complete
.BR fhicl::ParameterSet ,
and prints the parts of it that define an art job: the process name, the
source module type, the output modules, the services, the producers,
analyzers and filters, the
.B trigger_paths
and
.B end_paths
lists, and the paths.
.PP
A
.I path
is any name directly under
.B physics
other than the five reserved names
.BR producers ,
.BR analyzers ,
.BR filters ,
.B trigger_paths
and
.BR end_paths .
Each path is classified from the module labels it lists:
.IP \(bu 2
a label found in exactly one of
.BR physics.producers ,
.BR physics.filters ,
.B physics.analyzers
or
.B outputs
is trigger-eligible (producer or filter) or end-eligible (analyzer or
output); a label found in none or in several is ambiguous;
.IP \(bu 2
a path whose labels are all trigger-eligible is a
.IR "trigger path" ,
one whose labels are all end-eligible is an
.IR "end path" ,
and any other path, including an empty one, is
.IR ambiguous .
.PP
Classification runs for every invocation, whatever the verbosity.
A non-reserved entry under
.B physics
whose value is not a sequence (a table, for example) therefore makes the
program fail (exit 1) even when only the default summary was asked for.
.PP
Absent tables are shown as
.BR <not\ present> ;
in the
.B \-v
and
.B \-vv
listings, a table or list that is present but empty is shown as
.BR <present\ but\ empty> ,
and a module without
.B module_type
is listed with type
.BR <not\ present> .
.SS Output levels
.TP
default
One line each: file name, process name, source module type, and the
number of outputs, services, producers, analyzers, filters,
.B trigger_paths
entries,
.B end_paths
entries and candidate paths.
The services line is printed as
.B <not\ present>
whenever
.B physics.producers
is absent, and as a count otherwise; see BUGS.
.TP
.B \-v
Outputs as
.RI \(lq label " : " module_type \(rq,
services by name, the producer, analyzer, filter,
.B trigger_paths
and
.B end_paths
counts, then the path names grouped as trigger, end and ambiguous.
.TP
.B \-vv
As
.BR \-v ,
but producers, analyzers and filters are listed as
.RI \(lq label " : " module_type \(rq
and the
.B trigger_paths
and
.B end_paths
entries are listed.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-v
Verbose listing.
Must be the first of exactly two arguments.
.TP
.B \-vv
More verbose listing.
Must be the first of exactly two arguments.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print the usage line to standard output and exit 0.
Recognised only as the first argument.
.PP
With one argument, that argument is the file.
With two, the first must be
.B \-v
or
.BR \-vv ;
.B fhicl-summary job.fcl \-v
tries to open a file named
.B \-v
and fails.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I file.fcl
The top-level configuration, opened as given (relative to the current
directory or absolute).
Included files are looked up along
.BR FHICL_FILE_PATH .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B FHICL_FILE_PATH
Colon-separated list of directories searched for files named in
.B #include
directives (the
.B cet::filepath_lookup_after1
policy).
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The summary was printed, or
.B \-h
was given.
.TP
.B 1
Any error, with a message on standard error: wrong number of arguments or
an unrecognised option (the usage line is appended), the file cannot be
found or parsed, or a fhiclcpp lookup failed during classification.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.EX
export FHICL_FILE_PATH=.:/path/to/fcl/tree
fhicl-summary job.fcl
fhicl-summary \-v job.fcl
fhicl-summary \-vv job.fcl | less
.EE
.RE
.SH BUGS
At the default level the services count is guarded by the presence of
.B physics.producers
instead of
.B services
.RB ( fhicl-summary.cc:294 ).
A configuration with services but no producers shows
.B services:\ <not\ present>;
one with producers but no services shows
.BR "services: 0" .
Use
.B \-v
for a correct services listing.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR fhicl-getpar (1),
.BR fhicl-dump (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Rob Kutschke (2020).
Manual page written from
.B mu2ebintools/fhicl-summary.cc
for the Mu2e DAQ mega-review, 2026-10-06.
